# EXAMPLE: this file is not read. Copy it to "wifi.conf" in the same folder
# (netcast/mainline/ on the stick; no ".example" or ".txt" at the end) and edit the copy.
#
# Wi-Fi for Debian, with a USB Wi-Fi adapter on an Atheros AR9170 chip (carl9170 driver),
# e.g. the Netgear WN111v2. The TV's built-in Wi-Fi has no Linux driver.
# Remove the "#" in front of the lines below and fill them in. The name and the passphrase
# are taken exactly as written (spaces included, no quotes). No psk line = an open network.
# A full wpa_supplicant.conf also works.
#ssid=My network
#psk=my passphrase
#country=US
